 if the type of capacity is a reserved capacity type and a timing of the virtual machine request corresponds to a time period allocated to the user for reserved capacity with the specified amount of bandwidth, fulfill the virtual machine request using the reserved capacity; 
 if the type of capacity is an excess capacity type: 

       determining whether a bid price is a winning bid price, the winning bid price being greater than other pending bids for the same excess capacity and being at least equal to a current market price; and
 if the bid price is the winning bid price and excess capacity for the user with at least the specified amount of bandwidth is available, fulfill the instance virtual machine request using the excess capacity for at least a minimum period of time; 

       if the type of capacity is a variable capacity type and variable capacity is available, fulfill the virtual machine request using the variable capacity, the variable capacity capable of having less than the amount of bandwidth specified for the virtual machine request;
 if the dedicated capacity with the amount of bandwidth is not available for the virtual machine request specifying the dedicated capacity type, change the type of capacity specified by the instance request to one of an excess capacity type or a variable capacity type; 
 if the reserved capacity with the amount of bandwidth is not available for the virtual machine request specifying the reserved capacity type, change the type of capacity specified by the virtual machine request to one of an excess capacity type or a variable capacity type; 
 if the excess capacity with the amount of bandwidth is not available for the virtual machine request specifying the excess capacity type, changing the type of capacity specified by the virtual machine request to a variable capacity type; 
 if the variable capacity is not available for the virtual machine request specifying the variable capacity type, deny the virtual machine request; and 
 if the virtual machine request is being fulfilled using the excess capacity and the excess capacity becomes no longer available, move fulfillment of the instance virtual machine request to variable capacity if available. 



       10. The system of  claim 6 , wherein the time period corresponds to at least one of a fixed time window and a sliding time window associated with the user. 


