claims:
What is claimed is:  

       1. A method for determining the status of a GAD associated autoimmune disorder in a patient which comprises contacting T-cells of said patient with at least one peptide that is selected from the group consisting of: 
       (a) KPCSCSKVDVNYAFLHATDL (SEQ ID NO:06);  
       (b) NMYAMMIARFKMFPEVKEKG (SEQ ID NO:07);  
       (c) TAGTTVYGAFDPLLAVADICKK (SEQ ID NO:08);  
       (d) EYLYNIIKNREGYEMVFDGK (SEQ ID NO:09);  
       (e) IPPSLRYLEDNEERMSRLSK (SEQ ID NO:10);  
       (f) SRLSKVAPVIKARMMEYGTT (SEQ ID NO:11);  
       (g) EYGTTMVSYQPLGDKVNFFR (SEQ ID NO:12); and  
       (h) ATHQDIDFLIEEIERLGQDL (SEQ ID NO:13).  


       2. The method according to  claim 1 , wherein the response of the T-cell to contact with said at least one peptide is stimulation. 


       3. The method according to  claim 2 , wherein the stimulation is measured by cellular uptake of radiolabelled nucleoside. 


       4. The method according to  claim 3 , wherein the nucleoside is  3 H thymidine. 


       5. The method according to  claim 1 , wherein the disorder is IDDM. 


       6. The method according to  claim 1 , wherein the disorder is stiff man syndrome. 


       7. A method for detecting a GAD associated autoimmune disorder in a patient having or at risk of having the disorder, said method comprising contacting T-cells from said patient with a diagnostically effective amount of a diagnostically effective fragment of GAD 65  and detecting the response of said T-cells to said fragment of GAD 65  wherein said T-cell response is indicative of the presence of said disorder, wherein said diagnostically effective fragment is selected from the group consisting of: 
       (a) KPCSCSKVDVNYAFLHATDL (SEQ ID NO:06);  
       (b) NMYAMMIARFKMFPEVKEKG (SEQ ID NO:07);  
       (c) TAGTTVYGAFDPLLAVADICKK (SEQ ID NO:08);  
       (d) EYLYNIIKNREGYEMVFDGK (SEQ ID NO:09);  
       (e) IPPSLRYLEDNEERMSRLSK (SEQ ID NO:10);  
       (f) SRLSKVAPVIKARMMEYGTT (SEQ ID NO:11);  
       (g) EYGTTMVSYQPLGDKVNFFR (SEQ ID NO:12); and  
       (h) ATHQDIDFLIIEEIERLGQDL (SEQ ID NO:13).  


       8. The method according to  claim 7 , wherein the disorder is IDDM. 


       9. The method according to  claim 7 , wherein the disorder is stiff man syndrome. 


       10. A method for staging a β-cell associated autoimmune disease of a patient suspected of having a susceptibility to said autoimmune disease, said method comprising: 
       determining the autoreactivity of T-cells of said patient toward at least one peptide that is selected from the group consisting of:  
       (a) KPCSCSKVDVNYAFLHATDL (SEQ ID NO:06);  
       (b) NMYAMMIARFKMFPEVKEKG (SEQ ID NO:07);  
       (c) TAGTTVYGAFDPLLAVADICKK (SEQ ID NO:08);  
       (d) EYLYNIIKNREGYEMVFDGK (SEQ ID NO:09);  
       (e) IPPSLRYLEDNEERMSRLSK (SEQ ID NO:10);  
       (f) SRLSKVAPIKARMMEYGTT (SEQ ID NO:11);  
       (g) EYGTTMVSYQPLGDKVNFFR (SEQ ID NO:12); and  
       (h) ATHQDIDFLIEEIERLGQDL (SEQ ID NO:13).  


       11. The method according to  claim 10 , wherein the disease is IDDM. 


       12. The method according to  claim 10 , wherein the disease is stiff man syndrome. 


       13. A kit useful for determining the status of a GAD associated disorder in a specimen of a patient, said kit comprising one or more containers comprising a polypeptide that is IPPSLRYLEDNEERMSRLSK (SEQ ID NO:10).

