A light beam optical scanner, comprising: 
      a light source that emits a light beam;  
      a deflector having a plurality of deflecting facets that have widths smaller than a width of the light beam, at least two of the deflecting facets being irradiated by the light beam and deflecting the light beam;  
      an optical element that is disposed so that a deflected light beam is applied to the optical element, the deflected light beam being a beam that has been deflected by one of the deflecting facets, the optical element being one of a first optical element through which the deflected light beam passes and a second optical element that reflects the deflected light beam, an incident angle of the deflected light beam applied to an incidence plane of the optical element changing according to an angle of deflection at which the deflecting facet has deflected the light beam; and  
      a thin film with which at least one of an incidence plane of the first optical element, an incidence plane of the second optical element, an emission plane of the first optical element, and the deflecting facet is provided, reflectance and transmissivity of the thin film depending on the incident angle.

claims:
1. A method for forming a metal-oxide-semiconductor (MOS) device, the method comprising:
 providing a substrate; 
 forming a gate structure overlying the substrate; 
 forming a sidewall spacer on a sidewall of the gate structure, wherein the sidewall spacer has an L-shape and comprises a vertical leg and a horizontal leg; 
 forming a corner spacer comprising:
 a first portion on the substrate and adjacent an outer edge of the horizontal leg of the sidewall spacer; 
 a second portion on top of the vertical leg of the sidewall spacer, wherein the first portion and the second portion of the corner spacer are disconnected; 

 forming a source/drain region substantially vertically aligned with an interface between the sidewall spacer and the first portion of the corner spacer; and 
 forming a silicide region substantially aligned with an outer edge of the first portion of the corner spacer. 



     2. The method of  claim 1 , wherein the step of forming the source/drain region is performed after the step of forming the sidewall spacer and before the step of forming the corner spacer. 


     3. The method of  claim 1 , wherein the step of forming the silicide region is performed after the step of forming the corner spacer. 


     4. The method of  claim 1 , wherein the corner spacer further comprises a third portion on the horizontal leg and adjacent to the vertical leg of the sidewall spacer, wherein the first portion, the second portion, and the third portion of the corner spacer are disconnected from each other. 


     5. The method of  claim 1 , wherein the step of forming the corner spacer comprises:
 forming a dielectric layer over the sidewall spacer; and 
 etching the dielectric layer without using a mask to cover portions of the dielectric layer. 



     6. The method of  claim 1 , wherein the step of forming the sidewall spacer comprises:
 forming an oxide layer; and 
 forming a nitride layer over the oxide layer, wherein the corner spacer is formed of nitride. 



     7. The method of  claim 6 , wherein the step of forming the sidewall spacer further comprises:
 forming an additional oxide layer over the nitride layer; 
 performing an anisotropic etching to the additional oxide layer, so that a remaining portion of the addition oxide layer remains on a horizontal leg of the nitride layer; and 
 after the step of forming the source/drain region and before the step of forming the corner spacer, removing the remaining portion of the addition oxide layer. 



     8. A method for forming a metal-oxide-semiconductor (MOS) device, the method comprising:
 providing a substrate; 
 forming a gate structure overlying the substrate; 
 forming an inner oxide layer over the gate structure and the substrate; 
 forming a first nitride layer on the inner oxide layer; 
 forming an outer oxide layer on the first nitride layer; 
 etching the outer oxide layer, the first nitride layer, and the inner oxide layer using the outer oxide layer as a mask so that the inner oxide layer and the first nitride layer form a sidewall spacer having an L-shape with a vertical leg and a horizontal leg, and the outer oxide layer has a remaining portion on the horizontal leg of the first nitride layer; 
 implanting the substrate to form a source/drain region; 
 removing the remaining portion of the outer oxide layer; 
 blanket forming a second nitride layer; 
 etching the second nitride layer, wherein a remaining portion of the second nitride layer forms non-continuous corner spacers having at least one of a first portion and a second portion, and wherein the first portion is on the substrate and adjacent an edge of the horizontal leg of the sidewall spacer, and the second portion is on the horizontal leg and adjacent the vertical leg of the sidewall spacer; and 
 siliciding the source/drain region. 



     9. The method of  claim 8 , wherein the step of etching the outer oxide layer, the first nitride layer, and the inner oxide layer comprises plasma etching, and the step of etching the second nitride layer comprises dry etchings. 


     10. The method of  claim 8 , wherein an end point mode is used in the step of etching the outer oxide layer, the first nitride layer, and the inner oxide layer for detecting end points. 


     11. The method of  claim 8 , wherein the step of etching the second nitride layer comprises detecting an end point of the etching and continuing etching for an extension time after the end point is detected. 


     12. The method of  claim 11 , wherein the extension time is between about 3 seconds and about 30 seconds. 


     13. The method of  claim 8 , wherein the non-continuous corner spacers further comprise a third portion on the vertical leg of the first oxide layer. 


     14. The method of  claim 8  further comprising, after the step of siliciding, blanket forming a contact etch stop layer.

