I will create a hypothetical but plausible structure for a semiconductor device to demonstrate standard claim formatting.

A semiconductor device, comprising:
a semiconductor substrate;
a channel region formed within the semiconductor substrate;
a three-dimensional gate structure laterally encompassing the channel region;
a composite high-k gate dielectric layer disposed between the three-dimensional gate structure and the channel region;
a source region and a drain region formed in the semiconductor substrate adjacent to the channel region; and
a plurality of metallic contacts electrically coupled to the source region and the drain region, respectively, wherein at least one of the plurality of metallic contacts extends over a portion of the three-dimensional gate structure.

A method for stripping aluminum from a diffusion coating, the method comprising:
contacting a substrate having a diffusion coating thereon, said diffusion coating comprising aluminum, with a stripping solution;
wherein said stripping solution is an acidic solution comprising phosphoric acid and at least one fluoride-containing compound;
maintaining said contact at an elevated temperature for a time sufficient to remove at least a portion of the aluminum from said diffusion coating; and
subsequently rinsing said substrate to remove said stripping solution and stripped aluminum.

A universal locker system, comprising:
a plurality of individually lockable storage compartments;
an electronic locking mechanism associated with each of the plurality of individually lockable storage compartments;
a central locker management controller coupled to each electronic locking mechanism;
at least one user interface module coupled to the central locker management controller, the at least one user interface module configured to receive an access credential from a user;
a display unit coupled to the central locker management controller, the display unit configured to present information to a user; and
a communication interface coupled to the central locker management controller, the communication interface configured to communicate with a remote server;
wherein the central locker management controller is configured to:
receive the access credential from the at least one user interface module;
validate the received access credential;
dynamically assign one of the plurality of individually lockable storage compartments to the user based on the validated access credential and an availability status of the plurality of individually lockable storage compartments; and
electronically control unlocking of the assigned individually lockable storage compartment via its associated electronic locking mechanism upon successful validation of the access credential.

A system for processing images by selecting appropriate document size, the system comprising:
an image input interface configured to receive image data;
a processing unit coupled to the image input interface;
a memory coupled to the processing unit, the memory storing instructions and a plurality of predefined document size criteria;
the processing unit being configured to execute instructions to:
analyze the received image data to determine one or more characteristics of the image content;
compare the determined image characteristics with the stored predefined document size criteria;
select an appropriate document size from a plurality of available document sizes based on the comparison;
process the image data according to the selected document size; and
output the processed image data.

A disk drive comprising:
