A method for distributing high and low-bandwidth voice channels using a minimum number of timeslots, comprising:
identifying a plurality of voice channels, said plurality of voice channels comprising at least one high-bandwidth voice channel and at least one low-bandwidth voice channel;
determining a bandwidth requirement for each of the plurality of voice channels;
allocating the plurality of voice channels to a set of available timeslots by:
    assigning each identified high-bandwidth voice channel to at least one dedicated timeslot based on its determined bandwidth requirement; and
    multiplexing a plurality of identified low-bandwidth voice channels into a shared timeslot based on their determined bandwidth requirements;
wherein said allocating minimizes a total number of timeslots utilized for transmitting the identified plurality of voice channels; and
transmitting the allocated plurality of voice channels within the minimized total number of timeslots.

A capstan assembly for a normal belt, comprising:
