and providing, by the electronic bill payment and presentment system, a payment status update to at least one of the payee or the biller.

A data processing device, comprising:
a processor core configured to execute instructions;
a memory system coupled to the processor core, configured to store instructions and data;
an instruction decoder, coupled to the processor core and the memory system, configured to retrieve and decode instructions from the memory system;
at least one general-purpose register, accessible by the processor core, configured to store data and address pointers, including at least one index register;
an arithmetic logic unit (ALU), coupled to the processor core and the at least one general-purpose register, configured to perform arithmetic operations;
wherein the instruction decoder is further configured to decode an instruction specifying an indexed immediate addressing mode;
the instruction comprising an opcode, an immediate value, and a specification of a particular index register from the at least one index register;
wherein, upon decoding the instruction specifying the indexed immediate addressing mode, the processor core is configured to cause the ALU to add the immediate value from the instruction to a content of the particular index register to generate an effective memory address;
and wherein the processor core is further configured to use the generated effective memory address to access data in the memory system.

A method for managing bandwidth utilization for a plurality of shared resources, the method comprising:
identifying a plurality of shared resources, each shared resource having an associated total available bandwidth;
identifying a plurality of entities requesting access to at least one of the plurality of shared resources;
establishing one or more bandwidth allocation policies defining criteria for allocating bandwidth among the plurality of entities for the plurality of shared resources;
allocating a portion of the total available bandwidth of each requested shared resource to each requesting entity based on the one or more bandwidth allocation policies;
monitoring actual bandwidth utilization by each of the plurality of entities for each of the plurality of shared resources; and
dynamically adjusting the allocated bandwidth to at least one of the plurality of entities for at least one of the plurality of shared resources based on the monitored actual bandwidth utilization and the one or more bandwidth allocation policies;
whereby bandwidth contention is reduced and resource performance is optimized.

A method for side impact testing of motor vehicles at a sub-system level, comprising:
providing a motor vehicle sub-system, wherein the sub-system comprises a structural component or assembly of a motor vehicle side structure configured to interact with an occupant during a side impact event;
mounting the motor vehicle sub-system onto a test fixture, wherein the test fixture is configured to simulate structural boundary conditions experienced by the sub-system when integrated within a full motor vehicle during a side impact;
applying an impact force to the mounted motor vehicle sub-system using an impactor, wherein the impactor is configured to replicate a load profile or a deformation profile characteristic of a full vehicle side impact event;
measuring at least one impact-related parameter associated with the sub-system during the application of the impact force; and
analyzing the measured impact-related parameter to assess the side impact performance of the motor vehicle sub-system.

A method for determining network topologies, comprising:
  transmitting a plurality of probe signals from a computing device to a plurality of network devices within a network;
  receiving, by said computing device, a plurality of response signals from said plurality of network devices, wherein said response signals comprise topology information indicative of device identities and connectivity characteristics of said network devices;
  processing, by said computing device, said received response signals to identify said plurality of network devices and to identify inter-device connections therebetween; and
  generating, by said computing device, a network topology representation based on said identified network devices and said identified inter-device connections.

A protected prong file fastener, comprising:
