identifying a specific member from the plurality of members for temporary disabling;
receiving a command to temporarily disable the specific member or detecting a condition triggering said temporary disabling;
modifying a configuration associated with the VCG to designate the specific member as temporarily out-of-service;
rerouting data traffic previously traversing the specific member to be distributed among remaining active members of the VCG;
maintaining operational status of the remaining active members of the VCG during said temporary disabling;
monitoring for an enabling condition or a subsequent command to re-enable the specific member;
restoring the specific member to an active, in-service status within the VCG upon detection of the enabling condition or receipt of the subsequent command;
readjusting data traffic distribution to include the restored specific member as part of the active VCG.

