Here is a patent claim 1 for "Method and system for order returns," structured as a method claim:

1.  A computer-implemented method for managing order returns, the method comprising:
    receiving, by a computing device, an electronic return request from a customer, the electronic return request associated with a previously placed order and including identifying information for at least one item from the order and a stated reason for return;
    determining, by the computing device, based on predefined return policies and the identifying information, whether the return request is authorized;
    in response to determining the return request is authorized, generating, by the computing device, electronic return instructions for the customer, the electronic return instructions including a unique return authorization number and a shipping label for returning the at least one item to a designated return facility;
    tracking, by the computing device, a status of the returned at least one item using the unique return authorization number;
    receiving, by the computing device, an electronic confirmation of receipt of the returned at least one item at the designated return facility;
    in response to the electronic confirmation, verifying, by the computing device, a condition of the returned at least one item against predetermined criteria; and
    based on the verification, initiating, by the computing device, a financial transaction corresponding to a refund or credit for the returned at least one item and updating an inventory record for the at least one item.

