A method for decentralized web annotation, the method comprising:
receiving, by a client device, user input identifying a target portion of web content displayed within a web browser application;
receiving, by the client device, annotation data associated with the identified target portion;
generating, by the client device, an annotation record comprising the annotation data, metadata associated with a user, and a content identifier unambiguously referencing the target portion of web content, wherein the content identifier is independent of a hosting server of the web content;
digitally signing, by the client device, the annotation record using a cryptographic key associated with the user;
transmitting, by the client device, the digitally signed annotation record for distributed storage on a decentralized network, wherein the decentralized network maintains a distributed ledger of annotation records;
in response to displaying the web content within a web browser application on a client device, querying the decentralized network for annotation records associated with the content identifier of the web content;
receiving, by the client device, one or more retrieved digitally signed annotation records from the decentralized network;
verifying, by the client device, the digital signature of each of the one or more retrieved annotation records; and
displaying, by the client device, the verified one or more retrieved annotation records as an overlay or integrated element within the web browser application in association with the target portion of the web content.

