at least one vehicle interface element extending from the main body, said at least one vehicle interface element configured to precisely engage a datum surface on the vehicle body to establish a fixed alignment of the jig relative to the vehicle; and
an automatic system interface portion integrated with the main body, said automatic system interface portion configured to mechanically couple with an end effector of the automatic system for manipulation and control of the jig;
wherein, when the door hinge is received in the hinge reception portion and the at least one vehicle interface element engages the datum surface on the vehicle body, the door hinge is held in a precise mounting position relative to the vehicle for subsequent attachment by the automatic system.

Here is a patent claim 1 for the given invention title, formatted as requested:

An apparatus for triggering a sliding and hinged sun roof, comprising:
a user input device configured to receive a user command for a sun roof panel, the user command indicating a desired movement selected from a sliding movement and a hinging movement;
a control unit electronically coupled to the user input device, the control unit configured to interpret the user command;
a sun roof assembly comprising the sun roof panel, a sliding rail system for enabling the sliding movement of the sun roof panel relative to a roof opening, and a hinge mechanism for enabling the hinging movement of the sun roof panel relative to the roof opening;
at least one actuator mechanically coupled to the sun roof assembly and electronically coupled to the control unit;
wherein the control unit is further configured to energize the at least one actuator to initiate the desired movement of the sun roof panel, such that the sun roof panel either performs the sliding movement along the sliding rail system or performs the hinging movement via the hinge mechanism, based on the interpreted user command.

A firearm trigger mechanism, comprising:
a housing configured to be mounted within a firearm frame;
a trigger pivotally mounted within the housing, the trigger having an engagement surface;
a sear pivotally mounted within the housing, the sear configured to engage a hammer or striker of the firearm, wherein the sear is operably coupled to the engagement surface of the trigger;
a trigger pull weight adjustment mechanism, including an adjustment screw threadably engaged with the housing and positioned to exert variable pressure on a spring biasing at least one of the trigger and the sear;
a trigger travel adjustment mechanism, including at least one adjustment screw threadably engaged with the housing and configured to limit a range of pivotal movement of the trigger;
wherein rotation of the adjustment screw of the trigger pull weight adjustment mechanism varies a force required to disengage the sear from the hammer or striker; and
wherein rotation of the at least one adjustment screw of the trigger travel adjustment mechanism varies a distance of travel of the trigger.

A method for extruding tire rubber material, the method comprising:
providing a pre-mixed, unvulcanized tire rubber compound at a predetermined temperature;
feeding the pre-mixed, unvulcanized tire rubber compound into an extruder apparatus having at least one screw for plasticizing and pressurizing the compound;
forcing the plasticized and pressurized tire rubber compound through a shaping die to form an extruded profile having a predetermined cross-sectional shape suitable for a tire component;
cooling the extruded profile while maintaining its predetermined cross-sectional shape; and
collecting the cooled extruded profile.

A method for dynamic flow-based multi-path load balancing with quality of service assurances, comprising:
  receiving network traffic comprising a plurality of data flows;
  identifying a plurality of available network paths for transmitting the network traffic;
  associating a quality of service (QoS) requirement with each of the plurality of data flows;
  dynamically monitoring performance characteristics of each of the plurality of available network paths, wherein the performance characteristics include at least current load and available bandwidth;
  dynamically selecting, for each data flow, a target network path from the plurality of available network paths by evaluating the associated QoS requirement of the respective data flow against the dynamically monitored performance characteristics of the plurality of available network paths, such that the selection provides the associated QoS assurance for the respective data flow while balancing network traffic load across the plurality of available network paths;
  directing each data flow along its respective target network path.

A system for location positioning using a machine-to-machine (M2M) ecosystem, comprising:
a target M2M device configured to be associated with an asset whose location is to be determined;
a plurality of anchor M2M devices distributed within a defined area, each anchor M2M device having a known or determinable geographical position;
an M2M communication network communicatively coupled to the target M2M device and the plurality of anchor M2M devices, wherein the target M2M device and the plurality of anchor M2M devices are configured to exchange location-related data over the M2M communication network; and
a location determination unit communicatively coupled to the M2M communication network, wherein the location determination unit is configured to receive the location-related data from the target M2M device and the plurality of anchor M2M devices, and further configured to calculate a current geographical location of the asset based on the received location-related data.

A semiconductor memory device, comprising:
a main memory array comprising a plurality of memory cells arranged in rows and columns;
a redundant memory array comprising a plurality of redundant memory cells;
a defect address storage circuit configured to store at least one address corresponding to a defective memory location within the main memory array;
an address input circuit configured to receive an input address for accessing a memory location; and
an address control circuit coupled to the address input circuit, the defect address storage circuit, the main memory array, and the redundant memory array, the address control circuit configured to compare the input address with the at least one stored defective address and, upon a match, select a memory location within the redundant memory array for access instead of the defective memory location within the main memory array, and upon no match, select a memory location within the main memory array for access.

A method for diagnosing electrical cables, comprising:
exposing an electrical cable to a penetrating energy beam;
acquiring projection data by detecting the penetrating energy beam after passing through the electrical cable, wherein the acquisition is performed from multiple angular positions around a longitudinal axis of the electrical cable;
generating a tomographic reconstruction of a cross-sectional image of the electrical cable based on the acquired projection data;
analyzing the tomographic reconstruction to identify a structural characteristic, degradation, or defect within the electrical cable; and
generating a diagnostic assessment of the electrical cable based on the identified structural characteristic, degradation, or defect.

A system for ship propulsion, the system comprising:
an airborne rigid kite body configured to generate aerodynamic lift and drag forces when exposed to an airflow;
an on-board power plant coupled to the rigid kite body, said power plant configured to generate power for operating at least one component of the airborne rigid kite body;
at least one active thrust generating mechanism coupled to the rigid kite body and powered by the on-board power plant, said active thrust generating mechanism configured to augment propulsion forces generated by the rigid kite body;
a tether having a first end coupled to the rigid kite body and a second end configured to be coupled to a ship, said tether configured to transmit propulsion forces from the rigid kite body to the ship; and
a control system configured to adjust flight parameters of the rigid kite body to optimize propulsion forces transmitted via the tether.

A computer-implemented method for an integrated system-of-systems modeling environment, the method comprising:
    providing a graphical user interface configured to facilitate user definition and configuration of a plurality of heterogeneous constituent systems, wherein each constituent system is independently operable and possesses distinct functionalities;
    receiving, via the graphical user interface, system definitions for each of the plurality of heterogeneous constituent systems;
    receiving, via the graphical user interface, interaction definitions specifying interdependencies, communication protocols, and interface specifications among the plurality of heterogeneous constituent systems;
    constructing a plurality of individual system models based on the received system definitions, wherein each individual system model represents the behavior of a respective constituent system;
    integrating the plurality of individual system models and the received interaction definitions into a unified system-of-systems (SoS) model, wherein the unified SoS model is configured to represent a combined operational behavior and emergent properties arising from the interactions of the plurality of heterogeneous constituent systems;
    executing the unified SoS model to simulate a dynamic behavior of the SoS under at least one defined scenario;
    analyzing simulation outputs from the executed unified SoS model to identify performance characteristics or emergent properties of the SoS that are not readily apparent from individual constituent system models; and
    presenting, via the graphical user interface, simulation results and analysis outputs related to the dynamic behavior, performance characteristics, or emergent properties of the SoS.

A system for a vehicle, comprising:
a display device disposed within the vehicle;
a plurality of input devices, wherein each input device is configured to receive user input from a distinct user within the vehicle;
a processor operatively coupled to the display device and the plurality of input devices; and
a memory operatively coupled to the processor and storing instructions that, when executed by the processor, cause the processor to:
display a graphical user interface on the display device;
display a plurality of cursors on the graphical user interface, wherein each cursor of the plurality of cursors is associated with a respective one of the plurality of input devices;
receive input from each of the plurality of input devices;
control a position and/or state of each respective cursor on the display device based on the input received from its associated input device; and
facilitate interaction with at least one vehicle function or at least one graphical element of the graphical user interface via at least one of the plurality of cursors.

A method for client-side scaling of web server farm architectures in a cloud data center, the method comprising:
acquiring, by a client device, server characteristic data for a plurality of web servers comprising a web server farm operating within a cloud data center, wherein the server characteristic data indicates an operational state or capacity of each of the plurality of web servers;
determining, by the client device, a web request distribution strategy among the plurality of web servers based on the acquired server characteristic data;
transmitting, by the client device, one or more web requests to at least one web server of the plurality of web servers according to the determined web request distribution strategy; and
periodically re-acquiring server characteristic data and re-determining the web request distribution strategy to dynamically adjust web request transmission based on changes in the operational state or capacity of the plurality of web servers.

A system for dynamically controlling the allocation of resources in a data processing system, the system comprising:
a resource monitoring module configured to obtain real-time usage data for a plurality of computing resources within the data processing system and to obtain demand data from a plurality of applications executing within the data processing system;
a resource analysis module coupled to the resource monitoring module, the resource analysis module configured to analyze the real-time usage data and the demand data to identify resource bottlenecks or underutilized resources, and to determine, based on said analysis, a modified allocation scheme for the plurality of computing resources; and
a resource allocation module coupled to the resource analysis module, the resource allocation module configured to apply the modified allocation scheme to control the allocation of the plurality of computing resources among the plurality of applications;
wherein the resource monitoring module, the resource analysis module, and the resource allocation module are configured to operate in a continuous feedback loop to adaptively adjust resource allocation based on changing usage and demand conditions.

An electrically conductive article, comprising:
