a timekeeping unit coupled to the time information extractor, configured to synchronize an internal clock based on the extracted time information; and
an output interface coupled to the timekeeping unit, configured to provide the synchronized time.

A retrofit clip for securing a first structural member to a second structural member for resistance against lateral and uplift forces, comprising:
    a unitary body formed from a high-strength material;
    a first attachment portion extending from the unitary body, the first attachment portion configured for mechanical coupling to the first structural member;
    a second attachment portion extending from the unitary body, the second attachment portion configured for mechanical coupling to the second structural member, wherein the first attachment portion and the second attachment portion are oriented at a predetermined angle relative to each other;
    a plurality of fastener apertures disposed through at least the first attachment portion and the second attachment portion, the apertures configured to receive fasteners for securing the clip to the first and second structural members; and
    wherein the unitary body is configured to be externally mounted onto an existing structural connection between the first and second structural members without requiring disassembly or significant modification of the existing structural members.

A system for analyzing network troubles using traffic track measurements, the system comprising:
one or more traffic measurement units configured to acquire network traffic data from a network, said network traffic data comprising information identifying a path of said traffic through said network;
a data storage device coupled to said one or more traffic measurement units and configured to store said acquired network traffic data;
a processing unit coupled to said data storage device and configured to analyze said stored network traffic data to identify network troubles, said network troubles comprising deviations from expected network behavior, network performance degradation, or network failures;
and an output unit coupled to said processing unit and configured to present an indication of said identified network troubles.

A self-contained payment system for facilitating transactions using digital vouchers, the system comprising:
at least one processing unit;
at least one memory unit coupled to the at least one processing unit, the at least one memory unit storing computer-executable instructions that, when executed by the at least one processing unit, cause the system to perform operations including:
  managing a plurality of digital vouchers, wherein each digital voucher is uniquely identifiable and represents a unit of intrinsic value within the system;
  maintaining a ledger of user accounts, wherein each user account is associated with a specific user and stores a current balance of digital vouchers held by that user;
  issuing a quantity of the digital vouchers into circulation by crediting a first user account with said quantity of digital vouchers;
  facilitating transfer of a specified quantity of digital vouchers from a sending user account to a receiving user account within the system in response to a payment transaction request, the facilitating including debiting the specified quantity from the sending user account and crediting the specified quantity to the receiving user account, thereby updating their respective balances; and
  processing a redemption request for a quantity of digital vouchers from a user account, wherein the processing includes debiting the requested quantity from the user account and removing the debited quantity of digital vouchers from circulation within the system.

1. An electronic device for providing a broadcast program, the device comprising:
a tuner configured to receive a broadcast signal;
a processor coupled to the tuner;
a memory coupled to the processor, the memory storing instructions executable by the processor;
an input interface coupled to the processor, the input interface configured to receive user input; and
an output interface coupled to the processor, the output interface configured to present program content;
wherein the processor is configured to extract program content and associated program guide information from the broadcast signal; generate an interactive program guide display based on the associated program guide information; cause the output interface to present the interactive program guide display to a user; receive, via the input interface, a user selection of a broadcast program from the interactive program guide display; in response to the user selection, control the tuner to tune to a broadcast channel corresponding to the selected broadcast program; and cause the output interface to present the program content of the selected broadcast program to the user.

A method for implementing trunk service based on Long Term Evolution (LTE) and a trunk user terminal (TUT), the method comprising:
establishing, by the TUT, a connection with an LTE network;
transmitting, by the TUT, a request to join a trunk group to a trunk service platform via the LTE network;
receiving, at the TUT, an indication of successful joining of the trunk group;
initiating, by the TUT, a push-to-talk (PTT) communication session by transmitting a PTT request signal to the trunk service platform via the LTE network;
receiving, at the trunk service platform, the PTT request signal;
establishing, by the LTE network, a dedicated radio bearer for the PTT communication session between the TUT and the trunk service platform, wherein the dedicated radio bearer is configured with quality of service (QoS) parameters optimized for real-time voice communication;
transmitting voice data, by the TUT, over the established dedicated radio bearer to the trunk service platform; and
distributing, by the trunk service platform, the transmitted voice data to one or more other trunk user terminals within the trunk group via the LTE network.

