A system for generating unique hardware identifiers for cloned virtual computing environments, the system comprising:
one or more processors;
memory coupled to the one or more processors;
storage coupled to the one or more processors and configured to store virtual machine configuration data and associated virtual machine images;
a generic physical location code generation module configured to generate generic physical location codes based on specific physical identifiers of a source virtual computing environment, wherein the specific physical identifiers comprise hardware addresses or unique identifiers associated with physical hardware components underlying the source virtual computing environment;
a configuration management module configured to associate the generated generic physical location codes with corresponding virtual components within a virtual machine configuration, wherein each generic physical location code provides an abstract representation of a physical resource's location or type without revealing its specific unique identifier;
an identifier assignment module configured to, during a cloning operation of the virtual computing environment, retrieve the associated generic physical location codes from the virtual machine configuration and, based on the retrieved generic physical location codes, generate and assign new, unique specific physical identifiers to virtual components of a cloned virtual computing environment, wherein the new, unique specific physical identifiers replace corresponding specific physical identifiers from the source virtual computing environment to prevent identifier conflicts within a network or virtualized infrastructure.

