A method for removing a base transceiver station from a wireless communication system, the method comprising:
    receiving a request to remove a base transceiver station (BTS) from the wireless communication system;
    initiating an offload procedure for user equipment (UE) currently served by the BTS, wherein the offload procedure comprises instructing the UE to transition its connection to one or more other BTSs within the wireless communication system;
    transmitting a deactivation command to the BTS, wherein the deactivation command instructs the BTS to cease transmitting and receiving wireless signals and to sever its logical connection with a core network of the wireless communication system;
    receiving a deactivation confirmation from the BTS;
    updating a network topology database to indicate the BTS as removed or inactive; and
    enabling physical disconnection of the BTS from the wireless communication system subsequent to receiving the deactivation confirmation.

