   a fault detection module coupled to said primary signal path, said fault detection module configured to identify a fault condition within said primary signal path;
   a switching module coupled to an output of said primary signal path and an output of said backup signal path, said switching module configured to designate one of said primary signal path and said backup signal path as an active signal source;
   an output port configured to supply an outgoing telecommunications signal from said active signal source; and
   a control module connected to said fault detection module and said switching module, said control module configured to, responsive to said fault detection module identifying said fault condition, instruct said switching module to shift the active signal source from said primary signal path to said backup signal path;
   wherein said system is configured to execute said shift in a manner that ensures said outgoing telecommunications signal remains substantially uninterrupted and substantially error-free during a transition period and subsequently.

