A method for decentralized web annotation, comprising the steps of:
receiving, by a client device, user input designating a target portion of web content displayed within a web browser application;
receiving, by the client device, annotation data pertaining to the designated target portion;
generating, by the client device, an annotation record containing said annotation data, user metadata, and a content identifier uniquely referencing the target portion of web content, wherein the content identifier functions irrespective of a hosting server of the web content;
digitally signing, by the client device, the annotation record employing a cryptographic key associated with the user;
transmitting, by the client device, the digitally signed annotation record to a decentralized network for distributed storage, wherein the decentralized network operates a distributed ledger of annotation records;
upon presentation of the web content within a web browser application on a client device, initiating a query to the decentralized network for annotation records corresponding to the content identifier of the web content;
receiving, by the client device, one or more relevant digitally signed annotation records from the decentralized network;
verifying, by the client device, the digital signature of each of the one or more received annotation records; and
displaying, by the client device, the verified annotation records as an overlay or integrated element within the web browser application in conjunction with the target portion of the web content.

