    a hydraulic actuator fluidly coupled to the control valve, the hydraulic actuator configured to receive the directed pressurized hydraulic fluid and, responsive thereto, generate a steering force; and
    a steering linkage mechanically coupled to the hydraulic actuator, the steering linkage configured to transmit the steering force to a steerable wheel of the vehicle.

A computer-implemented method for adapting a policy analysis workbench initially configured for privacy policies to operate across varied policy domains, comprising:
receiving, by one or more processors, multiple policy documents pertaining to a designated non-privacy policy domain;
analyzing the received policy documents for extracting policy statements, obligations, and constraints;
creating a dynamic domain-specific policy model and an associated ontology using the extracted policy statements, obligations, and constraints, said policy model being tailored for the specific non-privacy policy domain, this creation leveraging a framework derived from a sparcle privacy policy workbench architecture;
employing a series of sparcle-based analytical techniques on the domain-specific policy model to uncover instances of compliance issues, conflicts between policy statements, redundancies, or gaps within the documents for the non-privacy policy domain;
formulating, informed by these identified issues, conflicts, redundancies, or gaps, relevant policy insights for the designated non-privacy policy domain;
and thereafter presenting these policy insights through a user interface of the policy analysis workbench.

